Z||000000||Formula||06-21-2001||12:17 AM||||ok, me and my gf of 7 months got into it.  originally we went out and she slept with her ex after 2 weeks and she begged me to keep going out with her.  I said alright it was a mistake blah blah blah, in general I was nice about it.  Then in the second month that we went out everything was perfect, it was so great that i thought it would never end, then something happened and we became detached from each other, in the third month she got completly plastered at a party and made out with another guy, I of course dumped her but we eventually started going out again, but we never kissed or got close anymore, then in the fourth month we had a big argument about my ex gf and she acted like she was going out with the one guy at the before mentioned party.  but I was nice about it because I felt bad about blowing up and everything for the last time it happened but I was determined to break up with her.  When I went to her house to break up with her she apologized and asked if I wanted to try again and I said sure.  then we have been fine except for little arguments until now.  She had the house to herself and her step-brothers dad's friend (hes 20) and her met at a funeral because her step-brothers dad tries to cause problems at his ex wifes house.  well, he ended up getting her number and calling and he went to her house with a couple friends and they spent the night, which I was the only person who was supposed to be there with her according to her dad.  I was cool about it until the next night they did it again and she never stopped talking about how cool he was.  so me, being jealous, confront her about it (Im soft spoken btw) and she says it would be best if we break up for a while, because she says I dont trust her because I got on her case about spending the night with other guys,  I honestly probably dont trust her that much but I really want to try, so I told her that we can clean off the slate and start over so we can trust each other, but now she keeps saying that she needs to think about it everytime I ask her if she wants to go out again.  Im thinking to myself that I gave her a lot of chances and I ask for one more chance and she is rejecting me, and btw, she pretty much needs me for transportation and I'm almos the only guy that her dad trusts to take her out.  so if we break up she might be screwed and have to go back to early curfews and everything.<P>part 2, ok, heres the kicker, theres a girl that supposed to be really nice and a sweatheart, and shes pretty, not as pretty as the above girl but nice looking, and everyone says that we would get along perfect and that we deserve each other because we are both in relationships where we give it our all and get nothing in return.  I've only met her twice but she seems nice and she thinks I'm good looking and I think shes pretty, and we both just want to have fun, and I guess we are both nice, so what should I do?<P>I need advice about girls a lot lol. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierospeeder||06-21-2001||12:47 AM||||thought my g/f had problems.  Uh yours is worse.  <P>It would be different if she went out with a guy, but its a different story if she sleeps with him.<P>I would only have a phone friendship with her, and once a cheater, always a cheater.  She will be calling you within a week asking you for a ride to get pot or to go to work.  <P>I wouldn't get into a serious relationship with her, you will get hurt over and over again.  The way to get her off your mind is to think of all the negatives, sleeps around, cheats etc... makes you realize its not worth it.<P>||||reg||1
