Z||000023||Songman||06-21-2001||10:11 PM||||You're right... it will be tough. Print out my 9 year experience and every time you start to miss her read it. If you want I can send you the long version with all the gorry details...<P>And while I am posting here again, I do want to add this... There is a difference in being aware that bad things can happen in relationship and not trusting anyone. Even after all that I have been through I still choose to trust people. If you don't, when a good one comes along you will push her away with your attitude.<P>As I have said before, I believe the old adage that 'It is better to have loved and lost than never to have loved at all'. It just don't feel like it for a while right after you have lost in love. But I promise you that another one will come along for you. I speak from experience.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||7
Z||000024||FieroLisa||06-21-2001||10:22 PM||||Get over Girl #1.... No more chances, none, no, step away from the girl. <P>There's a REASON you don't trust her, so there's no reason you should feel guilty about it.<P>Go for Girl #2. Who cares if she's not as good looking? Is your girl just for an accessory?? I didn't think so! Besides, if she's not the girl for you, you're not putting a ring on her finger by going out with her once.  So go out with this girl, make it known that you're not necessarily ready for any kind of commitment yet (because it doesn't sound like you are)  <P>Leave yourself open to meet people! Don't think you have to be attached to anyone! There is a lot of merit in the single life- finding yourSELF is so important and its hard to do when your overshadowed by your mate!!!!<P>OK I'm done rambling, good luck and let us know how it turns out!<P>Lisa||||reg||1
Z||000025||Formula||06-21-2001||10:27 PM||||also, girl #2 is working her a$$ to make ends meet for her family and has 2 jobs (shes the daughter of a underprivaledeged family), and ever guy she meets ends up treating her like crap (from friends perspective).  She isnt grubby or anything but you can tell that she is helping out her family by what there house looks like, if you know what I mean.  And if we would get a long good and everything then when Im out of college I think that her niceness and wil to help her family would pay off for the both of us.<P>girl #1, she made a wrong turn a couple years ago and ended up in lock up.  she was extremly heavy into drugs, sex, etc.. and she just got off parole when we were going out for a couple months, before she met me she was planning on going through the same ****  again after she got off parole, except she would go to jail this time.  but for some reason she must have thought it was cooler to hang out with me and I kept her out of trouble, everyonce in a while she gets tendencies to smoke pot and whatnot and I tell her that anything in moderation isnt that bad.  But if you would have met her a couple years ago and then met her today you would think shes a completly different person.  and honestly I think that if I stop hanging out with her shes going to go the wrong way again and I would feel like its my fault.  Before she had no feelings for other people whatsoever, but now it seems like shes starting to have some compassion, like she actually cries at night if she really hurt someones feelings.  but today when I talked to her she was talking about an ex who broke just about every bone in her body, and she was like he just started out slapping me and he said he would never do it again, and thats why shes worried about staying with me, but I said that I would never hit her, and I never have hit her and she said that it was just an example.  but she's been through some rough times, and i can see how some of her morales might not be straight but they are coming along.||||reg||1
Z||000026||p4n1c||06-21-2001||10:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B>its so hard, Im gonna be so lonely because I spent every minute of extra time I had with her   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Get used to it...  It happens, she's treating you poorly, so dump her.  Get to know the new one, maybe she's ten times better and you'll enjoy spending the extra time with her and not have to worry about the trust issues.<P>"There was a time when we were back and forth.. It wasn't easy..  <P>I guess we're back where we belong.  One thing for sure it wasn't strong."  - No Use for a Name<BR><P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4<BR>*Under Restoration*||||reg||1
