Z||000033||Ken Wittlief||06-22-2001||11:42 AM||||Whoa Formula! Big red flag is waving here.<P> I dont know if you realize it but you are doing the knight in shining armour/ damsel in distress thing with girl #1, and maybe that is whats behing you and girl #2 as well.<P>  not to sound cold hearted here: If you want to rescue people in trouble become a doctor, pyschologist, minister, join the Coast Guard, or spend your evenings voulenteering at the Open Door Mission (I am NOT trying to be funny here).<P>  the only basis for a sound long term meaningfull relationship is when BOTH people have their acts together as individuals - both are secure well rounded and stable on their own - THEN they can contribute to a relationship.<P>  This girl is in really bad shape and it is commendable that you have pulled her up out of the muck, as it were. But here is a stern warning from an older guy that has see a lot of really bad stuff happen to nice guys like you - Be a hero if you want to but not as part of your personal love interest reationship.<P>  A hero needs his mate to go back to for love and support. Your mate cant be the one that is standing there to support you and be the one that needs to be rescued at the same time. YOU WILL BOTH GO UNDER! SHE WILL PULL YOU DOWN!<P>  Im not saying you have to cut this girl off and let her flounder. You can be a friend to her, you can be a shoulder to cry on, you can invest your time and money in her. Someday if and when she gets her act together you can hand her off to her future husband. In the meantime - make it clear to her that you two will be friends only - and take your love life somewheres else.<P>  You dont have to explain it to her. Cut her loose emotionally - be her hero if you want to - but be her Fireman/policeman/minister type hero - not her knight in shining armour.<P>edit: or if it makes it easier for you, treat her like you would a little sister, or your daughter - you can still care about her, but not be romantically/sexually involved. It sounds like what she needs most is a big brother right now anyway.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000034||fierojunky||06-22-2001||11:57 AM||||Hey - i guess I'll put my 2 cents in too.  As for girl #1 - loose her.  Shes just going to keep hurting you - don't get back with her again - it will just make it that much harder the next time.  As for girl #2 - if its "arm candy" your looking for it will probably be like girl #1.  I have dated girls i would rate as a 10 and they tend to be B!TCHES.  Girl #2 what, mabey an 8 and is (in my experiences) a heck of alot nicer and alot more fun too.  My adivse then lose the arm candy.  ||||reg||1
